+## When beforeSession throws
+
+- `beforeSession` runs inside the `try` block, so a throw there reaches the same `catch`/`finally` as any other failure in the turn: the caller still receives the original rejection, `onError` fires with the thrown error, and `afterSession` runs. `afterSession` therefore cannot tell a session that never started from one that finished — what a hook can assume is how much of the turn happened: no tools were run, no provider was called, and the session carries no assistant entry ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L32)).
+
